  "question": {
    "text": "The reaction of white phosphorus on boiling with alkali in inert atmosphere resulted in the formation of product <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The reaction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> with excess of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>AgNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> in aqueous medium gives ________&nbsp;mole(s) of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ag</mi><mo>.</mo></math> (Round off to the Nearest Integer).",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>OH</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>PH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><munder><mrow><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>PO</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></mrow><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced></munder></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>PO</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mtext>&#160;mole&#160;</mtext></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>Ag</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mtext>&#160;excess&#160;</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><munder><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>Ag</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mtext>&#160;mole&#160;</mtext></mrow></munder></math></p>",
